# Wireworm — The sprite art

Wireworm's art is supplied with the project, under `assets/`. Six folders cover
the node, the data-worm, the cursor, and the three foes, and the build draws each
of those elements from its folder rather than from art of its own. Everything
else the game shows is drawn in code, and the last section of this file lists it.

## How the folders are organized

Each folder under `assets/` holds one PNG per frame, named by its frame index
(`0.png`, `1.png`, and so on). Every PNG is `SPRITE_SIZE` (`32`) by `SPRITE_SIZE`
with a transparent background in straight alpha, so only its drawn pixels are
opaque and each frame composites cleanly over the dark board.

| Element | Folder | Frames | Constant |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Node | `assets/node/` | 5 (`0`–`4`) | `NODE_FRAMES` |
| Data-worm | `assets/worm/` | 6 (`0`–`5`) | `WORM_FRAMES` |
| Cursor | `assets/cursor/` | 1 (`0`) | `CURSOR_FRAMES` |
| Glitch | `assets/glitch/` | 4 (`0`–`3`) | `GLITCH_FRAMES` |
| Dropper | `assets/dropper/` | 1 (`0`) | `DROPPER_FRAMES` |
| Corruptor | `assets/corruptor/` | 4 (`0`–`3`) | `CORRUPTOR_FRAMES` |

A tile is `32` units square, so a frame maps onto one tile at a scale of one. The
frames are pixel art and stay crisp at every scale the stage is fitted to.

## How they are loaded

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build loads the frames itself. Every URL it requests resolves against the
page rather than against the origin root, so the produced site runs unchanged
whether it is served from the root of a static host or mounted under a sub-path.
`vite.config.ts` serves the `assets/` tree from the project root in development
and copies the same tree into `dist/assets/` when the site is built, so a frame
reaches the produced site under the folder and file name this file gives it.
{{else}}
The {{engine.name}} engine provides the asset loader, documented in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. It resolves every path under one root,
`assets/`, relative to the page the build is served from, and it fetches and
decodes the file. The build loads each frame through that loader rather than
requesting a URL of its own, writing the path relative to that root:
`node/0.png`, `worm/3.png`.

The produced site serves every seeded frame under that root, so a path the loader
resolves reaches the seeded file at whatever base path the site is served from.
{{/if}}

## The node: `assets/node/`

Five frames: one per charge state, plus a second critical frame.

| Frame | Drawn for |
| --- | --- |
| `0` | A node at charge `0` |
| `1` | A node at charge `1` |
| `2` | A node at charge `2` |
| `3` | A node at charge `3` |
| `4` | The alternate critical frame |

Every node on the board is drawn from this folder, centered on its tile. A node
at charge `3` alternates frames `3` and `4` at `NODE_PULSE_FPS` (`6`) frames per
second, so a critical node visibly pulses. A node below charge `3` holds the
single frame for its charge.

## The data-worm: `assets/worm/`

Six frames: a two-frame pair for each of the three parts of a chain.

| Frames | Part | Drawn on | Rate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `0`, `1` | Head | The leading segment of a worm | `WORM_HEAD_FPS` (`5`) |
| `2`, `3` | Body | Every segment between the head and the tail | `WORM_BODY_FPS` (`6`) |
| `4`, `5` | Tail | The trailing segment | `WORM_BODY_FPS` (`6`) |

Each pair alternates at its rate while the worm is on the board. A worm of one
segment is a head, and it is drawn from the head pair alone.

The art faces right. A segment of a worm whose horizontal heading is left is
drawn mirrored horizontally, so the same frame serves both directions.

## The cursor: `assets/cursor/`

One frame, drawn centered on the cursor's position in the player band. It points
up and is drawn upright, never rotated.

## The glitch: `assets/glitch/`

Four frames, played as a loop at `GLITCH_FPS` (`10`) frames per second while the
glitch is on the board, so it reads as unstable. The loop runs whichever way the
glitch is darting.

## The dropper: `assets/dropper/`

One frame, drawn centered on the dropper's position as it falls.

## The corruptor: `assets/corruptor/`

Four frames, played as a loop at `CORRUPTOR_FPS` (`8`) frames per second while
the corruptor crawls. The art faces right, and a corruptor crawling left is drawn
mirrored horizontally.

## What is drawn in code

No folder covers the following. Each is rendered by the build, and the spec named
beside it fixes its behavior.

| Drawn in code | Fixed by |
| --- | --- |
| The board, its background, and the tinted player band | `specs/board.md`, `specs/overview.md` |
| A bolt in flight | `specs/cursor.md` |
| The arcs of a discharge | `specs/discharge.md` |
| The HUD, every screen, every menu, the level banner, and all text | `specs/ui.md` |
| The debug overlay | `specs/instrumentation.md` |
